&lt;p&gt;Join the team as Twilio&#39;s next Legal Services Manager.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the job&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a Legal Services Manager to join our Center of Excellence function within our larger Legal Operations Team. In this role, you will be responsible for reviewing and vetting high-volume, repeatable work across multiple facets of the Legal Team and serving as the initial legal point of contact. You will also support ad-hoc operational activities to make the Legal Team more efficient.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you’ll be responsible for the following:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Legal Support Requests &amp;amp; Commercial Contracts&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as a first point of contact for GTM and Telecom Carrier Relations colleagues and provide education and process guidance on commercial contracts and other legal inquiries&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review, vet, and provide timely responses to a high volume of incoming legal requests, including general legal questions, agreement negotiation requests, and other legal support needs, while ensuring adherence to internal processes and policies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Independently review and negotiate NDAs, SOWs, assignment and assumption agreements, transition services agreements, service orders, and other miscellaneous legal documents on Twilio&#39;s template and counterparty&#39;s template&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Legal Processes &amp;amp; Operations&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support law firm eBilling matter creation and configuration, and resolve escalations related to law firm invoices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be an operational expert on all processes that touch the Center of Excellence (e.g., Twilio&#39;s GTM-facing and telecom carrier-facing contracting processes, law firm billing-related processes)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute your knowledge and learnings from novel situations to the Center of Excellence Playbook&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support a range of ad-hoc operational projects and high-volume tasks across multiple legal functions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Twilio values diverse experiences from all kinds of industries, and we encourage everyone who meets the required qualifications to apply. If your career is just starting or hasn&#39;t followed a traditional path, don&#39;t let that stop you from considering Twilio. We are always looking for people who will bring something new to the table!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A bachelor’s degree&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience as a Legal Operations Analyst/Manager, Contracts Administrator/Manager, or Paralegal&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong working knowledge of commercial contracts and commercial contracting principles, including experience independently drafting and negotiating NDAs, SOWs, assignment and assumption agreements, transitions services agreements, and service orders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience using commercial contracting tools, including Salesforce, Conga, Microsoft Office Suite, Google Suite, Airtable, DocuSign, and Adobe Acrobat Pro&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience using AI, with a working understanding of how common LLMs (e.g., ChatGPT, Gemini, Claude) function and can be leveraged to make day-to-day legal work more efficient&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Outstanding communication skills, both written and verbal, and strong attention to detail with a customer-first attitude&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be a process-minded and oriented professional&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work in a fast-paced and ever-changing environment with minimal supervision&lt;/li&gt;
