&lt;div&gt;We are actively recruiting for this role to fill an existing vacancy. This position is needed to build the foundational AI/ML capabilities and common platform tooling that power intelligent engagement experiences across Twilio. You will influence the design and evolution of our company-wide ML/AI Ops foundation, ensuring every AI capability incorporates rigorous offline and online evals to maintain exceptionally high quality.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;You will drive improvements to managing LLM workloads across the company, while ensuring easy and compliant access to data for AI/ML exploration and product development. This role requires a builder mindset to bridge theoretical research, production-grade experimentation, and scalable, enterprise-quality software.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;In this role, you’ll:&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct deep-dive research into and implement state-of-the-art LLM inference and orchestration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify opportunities to leverage small language via fine-tuning/distillation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build ML systems that hold up at Twilio scale.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set standards and tooling for building evals across a range of AI/ML capabilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Rapidly acquire new technical skills and knowledge in a fast-paced, high-delivery environment.&lt;/li&gt;
